      "math_academy_id": "e-8384",
      "problem": "Evaluate $\\tanh{4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\tanh x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the second definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡4 & =\\frac{{e}^{2(4)}-1}{{e}^{2(4)}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{8}-1}{{e}^{8}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
